{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The transactional artifacts all describe this one trip: EV-TRIP-00102, EV-GPS-00102 and EV-FARE-00102 each carry trip_id TRP-00102, and the trace's first fix at 2026-07-19T11:23:30+08:00 matches the trip record's started_at. The rider therefore discharges the identification limb of POL-RD-08(a) and the debate proceeds on this trip's own evidence.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00102", "EV-GPS-00102", "EV-FARE-00102"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.first_ts",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On the field POL-RD-01 makes governing — gps_trace.trace_distance_km, 21.79 km — the excess over the 20.4 km optimal route is 1.39 km, which clears the 0.8 km absolute establishment limb. The 21.8 km figure on the trip record is a rounded convenience copy of the same measurement and is not cited for the threshold test.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00102", "EV-TRIP-00102"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's explanation — that the BKE was crawling near Dairy Farm so he came off via Upper Thomson — is unsupported by any record. EV-ADVIS-00102-01 is MISSING, carries weight_multiplier 0.0 and the issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and no advisory covers the BKE or the Upper Bukit Timah corridor for the 11:16-11:55 window. With no advisory on file, POL-RD-03 cannot be run, and under POL-RD-13 and POL-RD-08 the driver's uncited traffic assertion carries no weight: it can neither excuse the excess nor supply an amended optimal route.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00102-01", "EV-GPS-00102"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The only chat message is the driver's own — 'boss BKE quite jam, i go Upper Bukit Timah ok?', sent by the DRIVER at 11:29:04, read at 11:29:40 and never answered by the rider — and it carries no waypoint_hint. POL-RD-04 exonerates a detour only where the instruction comes from the rider and identifies a place or road specific enough to act on, so the rider-requested-detour route to exoneration is simply unavailable to the driver on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00102"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider must candidly accept the one fact that decides this case. The excess on the governing trace is 6.81% of the optimal distance, below the 20% limb of POL-RD-01, and POL-RD-01 requires BOTH the percentage limb and the 0.8 km limb to pass. The distance deviation is therefore not established on the trace, and the POL-RD-02 distance-and-time refund is not triggered. The rider does not press a refund the threshold does not support; the concession is made because the record, not the rider's preference about the route, governs.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00102"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: on the disputed trip of 19 July 2026 (Woodlands to ION Orchard), the governing measurement under POL-RD-01 is gps_trace.trace_distance_km = 21.79 km against a booked optimal route of 20.4 km, an excess of 1.39 km, or 6.81% of optimal (EV-GPS-00102, EV-TRIP-00102). POL-RD-01 establishes a route deviation only where the excess is greater than 20% of optimal AND greater than 0.8 km; both tests must pass. The 1.39 km excess clears the 0.8 km absolute limb but falls well short of the 20% limb, so no deviation exists and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the route. The rider's assertion that the 0.8 km limb is cleared is accepted as far as it goes, but it cannot carry the claim on its own; the rider's own concession that 6.81% is below the 20% gate is correct and is the basis of this ruling. POL-RD-02's recomputation is therefore not engaged: the precomputed $2.45 refund figure on EV-FARE-00102 does not issue, and the $29.91 charged (EV-FARE-00102) stands as paid. Under POL-RD-08 the rider carries the initial burden and has not met the threshold, so the burden never shifts to the driver. The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes — 193 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps (EV-GPS-00102, POL-RD-07) — so the case is decided on the measured trace rather than escalated. On the driver's traffic explanation (BKE crawling near Dairy Farm, diversion via Upper Thomson): no traffic advisory is on file. EV-ADVIS-00102-01 is MISSING, carries weight_multiplier 0.0 and the issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and no advisory covers the BKE or the Upper Bukit Timah corridor for the 11:16–11:55 window. Under POL-RD-13 and POL-RD-08 that assertion is unsupported and carries no weight; because the driver cited no advisory ID, the missing advisory is not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact and does not escalate under POL-RD-10(5). The assertion is in any event moot, since no deviation is established. The single chat message ('boss BKE quite jam, i go Upper Bukit Timah ok?') came from the driver, not the rider, and carries no waypoint_hint, so the rider-requested-detour route under POL-RD-04 is unavailable; this too does not change the result. No billing-integrity issue arises: there are no ERP gantries and no airport surcharge (EV-FARE-00102). The driver's billed distance (21.8 km) is not less than the trace (21.79 km), so no POL-RD-04 driver compensation is payable. Confidence is capped at 1.0, both deciding artifacts (EV-GPS-00102 and EV-TRIP-00102) carrying weight 1.0. The disputed $7.00, and the $29.91 charge, are unchanged; the monetary effect is nil, below the execution threshold."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
